how much</span> to ask about prices.<br/>This is not a yes or no question. It asks for information.<br/>You can use a singular or plural verb with <span class = \"strong\">how much</span>.<br/>When you ask about a second item, you can say <span class = \"italic\">What about \u2026 ?</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"2\",\"columns\":\"1\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">How...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"How much is it?<br/>How much are they?<br/><br/>How much is \u2026 ?<br/>How much are \u2026 ?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How much is this shirt?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How much are the socks?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What about the t-shirts?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Saying How Much Things Cost"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you say how much things cost, you talk about money.<br/>There are different ways to say an amount of money."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"2\",\"columns\":\"2\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What You Say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"$20<br/>$20.50<br/><br/><br/>$105<br/><br/><br/><br/>$105.50\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twenty dollars<br/>tweny dollars and fifty cents<br/>twenty fifty<br/><br/>one hundred and five dollars<br/>one hundred and five<br/>one o five<br/><br/>one hundred and five dollars and fifty cents<br/>one hundred and five fifty<br/>one o five fifty\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scarf"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cloth to keep your neck warm"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This scarf looks nice with your coat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when you shop for clothing and accessories."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thing to wear around your neck with your business suit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He always wears a tie to work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "yellow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the color of a lemon"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She has a yellow umbrella."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "black"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the color of the sky at night"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He always wears black shoes. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "red"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the color of blood"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have an red and black scarf."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le05ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look online or in a store at accessories."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at scarves, ties, gloves and belts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find a good price for each item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find a high price for each i